Table full name: bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2011
Column name: year Type: INT64 Description: Year of the actual time of observation at which the barometer is read. It is 4-digit
Column name: month Type: INT64 Description: Month of the actual time of observation at which the barometer is read. (1=January, 2=February, …, 12=December)
Column name: day Type: INT64 Description: Day of the actual time of observation at which the barometer is read. Days 1-31
Column name: hour Type: FLOAT64 Description: Hour of the actual time of observation at which the barometer is read. Hours 0.00 to 23.99
Column name: latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Position to hundredths of a degree +N or –S (measured north or south of the equator) and +E or −W (measured east or west of the Greenwich Meridian).
Column name: longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Position to hundredths of a degree +N or –S (measured north or south of the equator) and +E or −W (measured east or west of the Greenwich Meridian).
Column name: imma_version Type: INT64 Description: IMMA Version: 0=2010, 1=2016
Column name: attm_count Type: INT64 Description: The attm count: 0 – abbreviated record (no attm) 1 – one attm 2 – two attms etc.
Column name: time_indicator Type: INT64 Description: Time indicator preserves the incoming precision of time fields: 0 – nearest whole hour 1 – hour to tenths 2 – hour plus minutes 3 – high resolution (e.g., hour to hundredths)
Column name: latlong_indicator Type: INT64 Description: Latlong indicator preserves the precision at which LAT and LON were recorded or translated from, or if they were derived later by interpolation between known positions: 0 – degrees and tenths 1 – whole degrees 2 – mixed precision 3 – interpolated 4 – degrees and minutes 5 – high resolution data (e.g., degrees to seconds) 6 – other
Column name: ship_course Type: INT64 Description: True direction of resultant displacement of the ship during the three hours preceding the time of observation (i.e., ship’s course (true) made good): 0 – stationary (ship hove to) 5 – SW 1 – NE 6 – W 2 – E 7 – NW 3 – SE 8 – N 4 – S 9 – unknown
Column name: ship_speed Type: INT64 Description: Ship’s average speed made good during the three hours preceding the time of observation (beginning 1 January 1968): 0 – 0 knots  1 – 1-5 knots 2 – 6-10 knots 3 – 11-15 knots 4 – 16-20 knots  5 – 21-25 knots 6 – 26-30 knots 7 – 31-35 knots 8 – 36-40 knots 9 – over 40 knots.    Prior to 1 January 1968 a different code for VS, also with range 0-9, applied (Met Office 1948): 0 – 0 knots 1 – 1-3 knots 2 – 4-6 knots 3 – 7-9 knots 4 – 10-12 knots 5 – 13-15 knots  6 – 16-18 knots 7 – 19-21 knots 8 – 22-24 knots 9 – over 24 knots
Column name: national_source_indicator Type: INT64 Description: A field available for national use in identifying data subsets.
Column name: id_indicator Type: INT64 Description: ID Indicator indicates whether a callsign or some other sort of identification is contained in the ID field (and in R3.0 data, II should always be extant when ID information exists; whereas II should always be missing if ID is missing): 0 – ID present, but unknown type 1 – ship, Ocean Station Vessel (OSV), or ice station callsign 2 – generic ID (e.g., SHIP, BUOY, RIGG, PLAT) 3 – WMO 5-digit buoy number 4 – other buoy number (e.g., Argos or national buoy number) 5 – Coastal-Marine Automated Network (C-MAN) ID (assigned by US NDBC or other organizations) 6 – station name or number 7 – oceanographic platform/cruise number 8 – fishing vessel psuedo-ID 9 – national ship number 10 – composite information from early ship data 11 – 7-digit buoy ID (proposed)
Column name: callsign Type: STRING Description: Identification/Callsign
Column name: country_code Type: STRING Description: The country that recruited a ship, which may differ from the country of immediate receipt (C2, field 15) and may also differ from the ship’s registry
Column name: wind_direction_indicator Type: INT64 Description: Gives the compass (and approximate precision) used for reporting the wind direction: 0 – 36-point compass 1 – 32-point compass 2 – 16 of 36-point compass 3 – 16 of 32-point compass 4 – 8-point compass 5 – 360-point compass 6 – high resolution data (e.g., tenths of degrees)
Column name: wind_direction_true Type: INT64 Description: The direction (true) from which wind is blowing (or will blow), stored in whole degrees (i.e., 360-point compass; range: 1-360°), or special codes: 361 – calm 362 – variable, or all directions
Column name: wind_speed_indicator Type: INT64 Description: Wind speed is stored in tenths of a meter per second (to retain adequate precision for winds converted from knots, or high-resolution data). WI shows the units in which and/or the method by which W was originally recorded (0, 1, 3, 4 follow WMO Code 1855): 0 – meter per second, estimated 53 1 – meter per second, obtained from anemometer (measured) 2 – estimated (original units unknown) 3 – knot, estimated 4 – knot, obtained from anemometer (measured) 5 – Beaufort force (based on documentation) 6 – estimated (original units unknown)/unknown method 7 – measured (original units unknown) 8 – high-resolution measurement (e.g., hundredths of a meter per second)
Column name: wind_speed Type: FLOAT64 Description: Wind speed which is stored in tenths of a meter per second (to retain adequate precision for winds converted from knots, or high-resolution data)
Column name: visibility_indicator Type: INT64 Description: shows whether visibility was: 0 – estimated (or unknown method of observation) 1 – measured 2 – fog present (obsolete)
Column name: visibility Type: INT64 Description: Visibility (horizontal visibility at the surface in kilometers) according to WMO Code 4377 from which, in reporting visibility at sea, WMO (2009a; Reg. 12.2.1.3.2) states that the decile 90-99 shall be used (moreover Reg. 12.2.1.3.1: when the horizontal visibility is not the same in different directions, the shortest distance shall be given for VV): 90 – less than 0.05 kilometer 91 – 0.05 92 – 0.2 93 – 0.5 94 – 1 95 – 2 96 – 4 97 – 10 98 – 20 99 – 50 or more
Column name: present_weather Type: INT64 Description: WMO Codes 4677 (Table D3) for WW, and 4561 for W1: 0 – Cloud covering 1/2 or less of the sky throughout the appropriate period 1 – Cloud covering more than 1/2 of the sky during part of the appropriate period and covering 1/2 or less during part of the period 2 – Cloud covering more than 1/2 of the sky throughout the appropriate period 54 3 – Sandstorm, duststorm or blowing snow 4 – Fog or ice fog or thick haze 5 – Drizzle 6 – Rain 7 – Snow, or rain and snow mixed 8 – Shower(s) 9 – Thunderstorm(s) with or without precipitation
Column name: past_weather Type: INT64 Description: WMO Codes 4677 (Table D3) for WW, and 4561 for W1: 0 – Cloud covering 1/2 or less of the sky throughout the appropriate period 1 – Cloud covering more than 1/2 of the sky during part of the appropriate period and covering 1/2 or less during part of the period 2 – Cloud covering more than 1/2 of the sky throughout the appropriate period 54 3 – Sandstorm, duststorm or blowing snow 4 – Fog or ice fog or thick haze 5 – Drizzle 6 – Rain 7 – Snow, or rain and snow mixed 8 – Shower(s) 9 – Thunderstorm(s) with or without precipitation
Column name: sea_level_pressure Type: FLOAT64 Description: Amount of pressure tendency at station level during the three hours preceding the time of observation in tenths of hPa (i.e., millibars)
Column name: characteristic_of_ppp Type: INT64 Description: WMO Code 0200 for characteristic of pressure tendency during the three hours preceding the time of observation (A) (after WMO 2015).
Column name: amt_pressure_tend Type: FLOAT64 Description: Amount of pressure tendency at station level during the three hours preceding the time of observation in tenths of hPa (i.e., millibars)
Column name: indicator_for_temp Type: INT64 Description: Indicator provides information about the precision and/or units that the Core temperature elements were translated from: 0 – tenths °C 1 – half °C 2 – whole °C 3 – whole or tenths °C (mixed precision among temperature fields) 4 – tenths °F 5 – half °F 6 – whole °F 7 – whole or tenths °F (mixed precision among temperature fields) 8 – high resolution data (e.g., hundredths °C) 9 – other
Column name: air_temperature Type: FLOAT64 Description: Air temperature, Celsius
Column name: wbt_indicator Type: INT64 Description: WBTI and DPTI indicate which of WBT or DPT was measured or computed, and ice bulb conditions: 0 – measured 1 – computed 2 – iced measured 3 – iced computed
Column name: wetbulb_temperature Type: FLOAT64 Description: Wet-bulb temperature, Celsius
Column name: dpt_indicator Type: INT64 Description: WBTI and DPTI indicate which of WBT or DPT was measured or computed, and ice bulb conditions: 0 – measured 1 – computed 2 – iced measured 3 – iced computed
Column name: dewpoint_temperature Type: FLOAT64 Description: Dew-point temperature, Celsius
Column name: sst_measurement_method Type: INT64 Description: Shows the method by which SST was taken: 0 – bucket 1 – condenser inlet (intake) 2 – trailing thermistor 3 – hull contact sensor 4 – through hull sensor 5 – radiation thermometer 6 – bait tanks thermometer 7 – others 9 – unknown or non-bucket 10 – “implied” bucket [note: applicable to early ICOADS data] 11 – reversing thermometer or mechanical sensor 12 – electronic sensor
Column name: sea_surface_temp Type: FLOAT64 Description: Temperatures are stored in tenths of a degree Celsius.
Column name: total_cloud_amount Type: INT64 Description: Codes 0 to 9 (WMO Code 2700) show the total fraction of the celestial dome covered by clouds (irrespective of their genus). 0 – clear 1 – 1 okta or less, but not zero 2-6 – 2-6 oktas 7 – 7 oktas or more, but not 8 oktas 8 – 8 oktas 9 – sky obscured by fog and/or other meteorological phenomena
Column name: lower_cloud_amount Type: INT64 Description: 0 – clear 1 – 1 okta or less, but not zero 2-6 – 2-6 oktas 7 – 7 oktas or more, but not 8 oktas 8 – 8 oktas 9 – sky obscured by fog and/or other meteorological phenomena
